    "spine_order": "7",
    "value_type": "scalar",
    "unit": "currency/month",
    "threshold_unit": null,
    "label": {
      "en": "Minimum wage (Salario Mínimo Interprofesional) - monthly - frozen at 2018 level for indexing regional benefits"
    },
    "short_label": {
      "en": "$SMI2"
    },
    "description": {
      "en": "SMI2 is a technical variant of the national minimum wage (Salario Mínimo Interprofesional) that the model freezes at its 2018 monthly level (735.90 EUR at the latest of 12 recorded values since 2005-01-01), used to index certain regional minimum-income rules that reference 'the minimum wage' as a benefit ceiling without automatically following its later increases. It is used in bsarg_es for Aragón's benefit ceiling (ArithOp UpLim, '24 - Aragón: Benefit amount' — consistent with the pre-2022 Ingreso Aragonés de Inserción being capped at the minimum wage) and for the Basque Country's lone-parent complement (BenCalc Comp_perTU, matching the country report's '6.4% additional amount of the minimum wage' for lone-parent households). It also appears in the historical DefConst formula for Madrid's GMI upper limit ($bsarg_rg30_up_lim), whose current formula instead references the live $SMI."
    },
    "explanation": {
      "en": "EUROMOD function group: Constants: main"
    },
